// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 05 — Output config for this machine  (per-machine, NOT tracked by git)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Copy this file to `05-local-output.kdl` next to it; that name is gitignored.
// install/bootstrap.sh does the copy for you, and fills in a `scale` when the
// laptop panel needs one — see below.
//
// Why this file exists separately from 99-local.kdl
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// niri keeps output blocks in a list and resolves a connector with
// `.iter().find()`, so for any given output name the FIRST matching block wins.
// That is the opposite of binds and environment variables, where the last
// definition wins — which is what 99-local.kdl relies on by being included
// last. An `output` block in 99-local.kdl would lose to the one in
// 90-user-extra.kdl and be ignored without any error. So output overrides live
// here, in a file included FIRST. (niri 26.04, niri-config/src/output.rs.)
//
// The same rule means a block here REPLACES the matching one in
// 90-user-extra.kdl rather than merging with it: restate everything you want,
// including `position`.
//
// Scale
// ─────
// Nothing in the tracked config sets `scale`, so niri uses 1. That suits a
// ~140 dpi panel and is much too small on the HiDPI 3:2 panels in current
// laptops. bootstrap.sh works the dpi out of the panel's EDID and writes a
// scale here when one is wanted; roughly, it targets ~130 logical dpi:
//
//   141 dpi (1920x1200, 14")   -> 1
//   182 dpi (2160x1440, 14")   -> 1.5
//   259 dpi (3000x2000, 13.9") -> 2
//
// Example:
//
//   output "eDP-1" {
//       scale 1.5
//       position x=0 y=0
//   }
//
//   // An external monitor to the right of a 2160-px panel at scale 1.5,
//   // i.e. 1440 logical px — this is what 90-user-extra.kdl assumes is 1920.
//   output "DP-1" {
//       position x=1440 y=0
//   }
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
